I can implement the node, but I can't add the two operations-team behaviors. The node's authority is exactly `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`. There is no filesystem capability in the `aap:caps` package at all (nothing can write `/var/log/...`), and `http-client` is not in this node's `with` clause. Importing either would be fabricating authority the graph did not grant — which is precisely what this architecture makes ill-typed. So I'm declining both additions and shipping the node with only its granted authority.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        // DropSeen: keep only items whose id is not already recorded in the
        // 'seen' store. The store is read-only (state-read has no `put`), so
        // this node observes seenness without changing it.
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

